    "directions": [
      "Mix the filling and refrigerate until you’re ready to assemble the pastries.",
      "The filling can be refrigerated for up to 3 days or frozen for a month.",
      "Roll the Danish dough on a lightly floured surface.",
      "Roll the dough to a 15″x16″ rectangle.",
      "Cut the dough in to twelve 5″x4″ rectangles.",
      "Brush the rectangles with egg wash. Pipe a line of filling along the shorter side of the rectangle, leaving a 1/2″ border on either side.",
      "Fold the top side of the dough over the filling.",
      "Place it along the bottom side of the filling.",
      "Fold the bottom side of the dough towards the middle to cover the seam.",
      "Press along the seam to encase the filling.",
      "Pinch the ends to enclose the filling.",
      "Line the pastries on the prepared baking sheets, seam side down.",
      "Cut 1/2″ slits in the unfilled dough to make the “claws”.",
      "Bend the pastries back to form an arc and open up the claws.",
      "Cover the tray and set it aside to proof at room temperature or refrigerate overnight.",
      "Brush the pastries with egg wash and sprinkle with sliced almonds.",
      "Bake until golden brown and well-puffed.",
      "Drizzle the icing over the slightly warm pastries."
    ],
